// Title
dots — Provisioning Architecture

// Paste this into app.eraser.io (or the Eraser VS Code extension) to render.

// ---- Entry points -----------------------------------------------------
Owner [icon: user]
Stranger [icon: user]

Entry Points [icon: terminal] {
  bootstrap-mac.sh [icon: apple]
  bootstrap-public-linux.sh [icon: linux]
  linuxansible alias [icon: terminal]
}

// ---- Playbooks ----------------------------------------------------------
Playbooks [icon: settings] {
  mac.yml [icon: apple]
  linux.yml [icon: server]
  public-linux.yml [icon: server]
}

// ---- Shared roles (linux.yml + public-linux.yml only — mac.yml has no roles) --
Shared Roles [icon: layers] {
  packages [icon: package]
  shell [icon: terminal]
  node [icon: code]
  docker [icon: box]
  ssh [icon: key]
  dotfiles [icon: file]
}

// ---- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
Ansible Vault [icon: lock] {
  ssh_keys/id_* (encrypted)
  ansible/.vault_pass (gitignored, owner-only)
}

// ---- Targets ----------------------------------------------------------------
Targets [icon: monitor] {
  macOS Workstation [icon: monitor]
  vps / master-node / cp / dp [icon: server]
  localhost (public mode) [icon: monitor]
}

// ---- Flow: entry -> playbook --------------------------------------------
Owner > bootstrap-mac.sh: curl one-liner (macOS) — needs .vault_pass placed first
Owner > linuxansible alias: manual run (personal Linux)
Stranger > bootstrap-mac.sh: same curl one-liner (macOS, no vault password)
Stranger > bootstrap-public-linux.sh: curl one-liner (Linux only)

bootstrap-mac.sh > mac.yml: installs brew+ansible, clones repo, hands off
linuxansible alias > linux.yml: -i inventory/hosts.ini
bootstrap-public-linux.sh > public-linux.yml: installs ansible, clones over HTTPS

// ---- mac.yml: flat tasks, no shared roles --------------------------------
mac.yml > Ansible Vault: brew update, then try-decrypt a real vault file to
  confirm ownership (a stranger's dummy .vault_pass doesn't fool this)
mac.yml > macOS Workstation: brew bundle Brewfile (owner) or Brewfile.public (stranger), mise node/go, macOS defaults, install.sh

// ---- linux.yml: full personal path, all roles including ssh -------------
linux.yml > Shared Roles: packages, shell, node, docker, ssh, dotfiles
ssh > Ansible Vault: deploy automation key + FIDO2 keys to target
Shared Roles > vps / master-node / cp / dp: provisions the real inventoried hosts

// ---- public-linux.yml: same roles minus ssh, no vault ever touched -------
public-linux.yml > Shared Roles: packages, shell, node, docker, dotfiles
Shared Roles > localhost (public mode): provisions the machine you're on

// ---- dotfiles role always closes the loop --------------------------------
dotfiles > Targets: git clone this repo + run install.sh to symlink configs
